From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iwls <iwls@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:06:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: Increase memory limit (GetMoreRam in Madeira)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settings › Increase memory limit signs in to the Apple ID Madeira was
sideloaded with (two-factor code or SMS) and turns on Increased Memory
Limit for Madeira's App ID, or another App ID of the account, as
GetMoreRam does; reinstalling from the sideloader then brings the
entitlement. The password is used for the sign-in only and never stored.

The sign-in and developer-services requests are Impactor's plume_core and
omnisette (MPL-2.0), vendored into build/rppairing-ios/src/appleid so they
link into the existing libmadeira_rppairing.a (a second Rust static
library would duplicate std). Changes to the vendored files: module
paths; certificate verification turned on in the anisette client
(upstream disabled it); request/response logging (session tokens) and
two panics removed. ffi.rs gives Swift a C interface with one worker
thread per session; a panic in the vendored code becomes an error event.
TLS is rustls + ring, as idevice already uses.
